== room | NIGHT · TOMY'S ROOM | cozy student bedroom at night with fairy lights and papers on the bed | phone
tomy (worried): Quddus, the embassy says I need proof of funds. Is that like proof of life?
quddus (talk): Close. It's proof that you can pay for your tuition and your living costs while you study.
tomy (think): So like... a picture of my piggy bank?
quddus (talk): More like official documents. And each country sets its own amount and rules.

== cafe | NEXT DAY · BANK CAFÉ | modern café next to a bank with glass windows and plants | cafe +laptop
quddus (point): Usually it's bank statements, a sponsor letter with their statements, or a scholarship letter that shows what's covered.
> 1f4b0 | COMMON PROOFS | 1f4b3 Bank statements | 1f4e9 Sponsor letter + their statements | 1f393 Scholarship award letter
tomy (think): Some countries ask for money to stay in the account for a long time, right?
quddus (thumbs): Yes. Some want it there for weeks or months, and some use special accounts like a blocked account. Always read the official visa page.
tomy (worried): My uncle said he can lend me money for one day, just for the statement.
quddus (shock): No! Sudden big deposits look suspicious, and fake documents can get you banned. Be honest and plan early.
tomy (cheer): Honest money, early planning. Got it!
